cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "glm-tpu: GLM-5.3 FP8 inference on a 32-chip TPU v4 pod"
abstract: >-
  A multi-host inference engine for the GLM-5.3 FP8 mixture-of-experts model,
  written in native JAX with custom Pallas kernels, for a Cloud TPU v4-64 slice
  (32 TPU v4 chips on 8 hosts). It provides resident and four-chat batched
  serving, a local chat UI and an OpenAI-compatible API, and a graph-equivalence
  harness that checks refactors against recorded TPU programs.
authors:
  - family-names: Vitale
    given-names: Gianluigi
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-29
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/GianluigiVitale/glm-tpu"
keywords:
  - JAX
  - Pallas
  - TPU
  - mixture of experts
  - FP8
  - sparse attention
  - LLM inference
